<!--
  Canonical, extensionless URLs only. vercel.json sets cleanUrls:true, which
  308-redirects /foo.html to /foo, so the .html forms must never appear here.

  WHILE THE SITE IS A PREVIEW, every page below also carries
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">. That is deliberate, not an
  oversight: a crawler reads this sitemap, fetches the page, sees the noindex
  and declines to index it — which is exactly the intent until the domain moves.
  A link checker will flag "in sitemap but noindex"; expect that until launch.

  The URLs themselves are already correct for production, so launch is only:
  delete the robots meta tags (see DEPLOY.md), then add the two blocks below.

  /privacy and /terms are intentionally ABSENT pending legal sign-off:
    <url><loc>https://www.juttr.cc/privacy</loc>
         <changefreq>yearly</changefreq><priority>0.3</priority></url>
    <url><loc>https://www.juttr.cc/terms</loc>
         <changefreq>yearly</changefreq><priority>0.3</priority></url>
-->
